 {
  "coord": "8:71",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "term",
  "note": "\"glass cabinets\" uses the banned word cabinet for the glazed presses.",
  "replacement": "The besiegers, appalled by their own uproar and by the silence that followed it, drew back a little and looked in. The study lay before them in the quiet lamplight. A good fire glowed and crackled on the hearth, the kettle sang its thin song, a drawer or two stood open, papers were set out neatly on the business table, and nearer the fire the tea things were laid. It was the quietest room you could imagine, and, apart from the glass cupboards full of chemicals, the most ordinary in London that night."
 },
